3. HLD 


Browser --> Click --> Click service --> Ad database (get redirect URL for given AD id )
            Redirect(302) <---

When click service is called it also needs to log click from user

One simple solution is to store all click info , in a click db , have it connected to some query service which is called by advertiser to query
Clickdb needs to be write optimised so we can go with Cassandra, however the issue here is we also need efficient range queries clicks in a time range etc 
which is not possible optimally in most dbs including cassandra

So what we will do is some sort of pre-aggregation we will have a EMR type algo(ex Spark) which will reudce and aggregate cassandra data (in a 1 min granulity) and put in in some read optimised db (OLAP db ex Amazon Redshift), so query service will call that instead of click db

Spark needs some trigger we can use cron scheduler for every say 5 min

With spark we will have 5 min delay still 

A better solution is from click service we should create a stream (Kinesis/Kafka) which is than consumed by some aggregator (Flink/Spark) which stores the 
data in memory and flushes it every min to OLAP db

for Fault tolerance etc we can shard our kinesis (as well as have multiple shards for hot ones)